        <div class="relative max-w-[560px]">
          <a
            href="#eu"
            class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 h-7 pl-1.5 pr-3 rounded-full border border-border bg-white text-[13px] text-muted hover:text-text hover:border-border2 no-underline transition-colors"
          >
            <svg class="w-4 h-4" viewBox="0 0 20 20" aria-hidden="true">
              <g fill="#E0B000">
                <circle cx="10" cy="3.2" r="0.9" />
                <circle cx="13.4" cy="4.1" r="0.9" />
                <circle cx="15.9" cy="6.6" r="0.9" />
                <circle cx="16.8" cy="10" r="0.9" />
                <circle cx="15.9" cy="13.4" r="0.9" />
                <circle cx="13.4" cy="15.9" r="0.9" />
                <circle cx="10" cy="16.8" r="0.9" />
                <circle cx="6.6" cy="15.9" r="0.9" />
                <circle cx="4.1" cy="13.4" r="0.9" />
                <circle cx="3.2" cy="10" r="0.9" />
                <circle cx="4.1" cy="6.6" r="0.9" />
                <circle cx="6.6" cy="4.1" r="0.9" />
              </g>
            </svg>
            Hosted and operated in the EU
          </a>
          <h1 class="h-display text-[44px] md:text-[60px] leading-[1.02] mt-6 mb-5">
            From prompt<br />to customers.
          </h1>
          <p class="text-[17px] md:text-[19px] text-muted max-w-[44ch] leading-[1.5] mb-8">
            Connect a GitHub repository and every push deploys your static site to a pagedock.eu address over HTTPS. Servers in Germany, nothing routed through the US.
          </p>
          <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3">
            <a href={~p"/users/register"} class="btn-primary no-underline">
              Create a free account
            </a>
            <a href="#how" class="btn-secondary no-underline">See how it works</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="max-w-[1080px] mx-auto px-6">
    <section id="how" class="py-24 border-t border-border">
      <h2 class="h-display text-[30px] md:text-[40px] leading-[1.1] mb-3 max-w-[24ch]">
        Three things happen. You do one of them.
      </h2>
      <p class="text-[16px] max-w-[56ch] mb-12">
        There is no build pipeline to configure and no YAML to write. Pagedock takes the files in your repo and serves them.
      </p>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-4">
        <div class="card p-6">
          <div class="w-7 h-7 rounded-md bg-accent-soft text-accent font-mono text-[12px] flex items-center justify-center mb-5">
            1
          </div>
          <h3 class="text-text text-[16px] font-medium mb-2">Add your repository</h3>
          <p>
            Paste the URL of a public GitHub repo and pick the folder your site lives in — the root, <code class="font-mono text-[13px] text-text bg-raised border border-border px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">dist</code>, <code class="font-mono text-[13px] text-text bg-raised border border-border px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">public</code>, wherever your HTML is.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card p-6">
          <div class="w-7 h-7 rounded-md bg-accent-soft text-accent font-mono text-[12px] flex items-center justify-center mb-5">
            2
          </div>
          <h3 class="text-text text-[16px] font-medium mb-2">Get an address</h3>
          <p>
            Pagedock gives your site a subdomain like
            <code class="font-mono text-[13px] text-text bg-raised border border-border px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">
              portfolio.pagedock.eu
            </code>
            with a valid certificate. It's live as soon as the first clone finishes, usually under ten seconds.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card p-6">
          <div class="w-7 h-7 rounded-md bg-accent-soft text-accent font-mono text-[12px] flex items-center justify-center mb-5">
            3
          </div>
          <h3 class="text-text text-[16px] font-medium mb-2">Push to update</h3>
          <p>
            Add the webhook Pagedock gives you to the repo. From then on, every push to your branch replaces the live site. Old deploys are kept so you can roll back.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="eu" class="py-24 border-t border-border">
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-12 items-start">
        <div>
          <h2 class="h-display text-[30px] md:text-[40px] leading-[1.1] mb-3 max-w-[20ch]">
            Hosted in Germany, run from Poland.
          </h2>
          <p class="text-[16px] max-w-[52ch]">
            Most static hosts serve from a global edge but keep the origin, builds and your account data in the United States. Pagedock keeps all of it inside the EU, which is a simpler story to tell your clients, your DPO, or yourself.
          </p>
        </div>
        <ul class="list-none m-0 p-0 border-t border-border">
          <li class="fact">
            <span class="text-text font-medium">Servers</span>
            <span>Hetzner, Falkenstein and Nuremberg, Germany</span>
          </li>
          <li class="fact">
            <span class="text-text font-medium">Your files</span>
            <span>Stored and served from the same EU machines. No US CDN in front.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="fact">
            <span class="text-text font-medium">Account data</span>
            <span>
              Email and repo URLs only, in an EU database. No analytics scripts on your sites.
            </span>
          </li>
          <li class="fact">
            <span class="text-text font-medium">Operator</span>
            <span>
              A sole proprietorship registered in Gdańsk, Poland. GDPR applies to us the same way it applies to you.
            </span>
          </li>
          <li class="fact">
            <span class="text-text font-medium">TLS</span>
            <span>Automatic certificates for every subdomain, renewed without you noticing.</span>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

